    "summary": "JSCompiler does not recursively resolve typedefs",
    "description": "goog.provide('a.b.c');\r\n\r\ngoog.scope(function() {\r\nvar b = a.b;\r\nvar c = b.c;\r\n\r\n/** @typedef {string} */\r\nc.MyType;\r\n\r\n/** @param {c.MyType} x The variable. */\r\nc.myFunc = function(x) {};\r\n\r\n});\r\n\r\nresults in a compiler error.\r\n\r\ngiven that JSCompiler *does* recursively resolve other names, this appears to be a bug rather than an intended limitation."
